{
  "info": {
    "name": "Workflow Engine API",
    "description": "Complete API collection for the Workflow Automation Platform\n\n**Base URL**: http://localhost:3000\n**Authentication**: JWT Bearer Token\n\n## Quick Start:\n1. Register a new user or login\n2. Copy the accessToken from login response\n3. Set the `authToken` variable in Postman\n4. Test workflow CRUD operations\n5. Create and trigger workflows\n\n## Features Tested:\n- User Authentication (Register/Login)\n- Workflow Management (CRUD)\n- Webhook Triggers\n- Run History\n- API Key Management\n- Health Monitoring",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_postman_id": "workflow-engine-api-v1",
    "version": {
      "major": 1,
      "minor": 0,
      "patch": 0
    }
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{authToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Auto-set base URL",
          "pm.request.url.host = ['localhost:3000'];",
          "",
          "// Add timestamp for requests",
          "pm.globals.set('timestamp', new Date().toISOString());"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Global test for successful responses",
          "pm.test('Response status is successful', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]);",
          "});",
          "",
          "// Parse and validate response structure",
          "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 201) {",
          "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
          "    ",
          "    pm.test('Response has success field', function () {",
          "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('success');",
          "    });",
          "    ",
          "    pm.test('Response has data field', function () {",
          "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('data');",
          "    });",
          "    ",
          "    pm.test('Response has meta field', function () {",
          "        pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('meta');",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "authToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "workflowId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "runId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "triggerPath",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🔐 Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('User created successfully', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('User data returned', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Tokens provided', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.tokens).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.tokens).to.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Auto-set variables",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('authToken', jsonData.data.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', jsonData.data.user.id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"postman@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Postman123!@#\",\n  \"firstName\": \"Postman\",\n  \"lastName\": \"Tester\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "register"]
            },
            "description": "Register a new user account\n\n**Required Fields:**\n- email: Valid email address\n- password: Strong password (min 8 chars, uppercase, lowercase, number, special char)\n- firstName: User's first name\n- lastName: User's last name\n\n**Response:**\n- User profile data\n- JWT access token (15 minutes)\n- JWT refresh token (7 days)"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Login User",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Login successful', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('User profile returned', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.user).to.have.property('id');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.user).to.have.property('email');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.user).to.have.property('fullName');",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Authentication tokens provided', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.tokens).to.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.tokens).to.have.property('refreshToken');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.tokens).to.have.property('expiresIn');",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Auto-set auth token for subsequent requests",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('authToken', jsonData.data.tokens.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('userId', jsonData.data.user.id);",
                  "    ",
                  "    console.log('✅ Authentication token set for collection');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"demo@test.com\",\n  \"password\": \"Demo123!@#\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Authenticate user and get JWT tokens\n\n**Credentials:**\n- email: demo@test.com\n- password: Demo123!@#\n\n**Response:**\n- User profile with roles\n- Access token (15 min expiry)\n- Refresh token (7 day expiry)\n\n**Auto-sets:** authToken variable for collection"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get User Profile",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Profile retrieved successfully', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('id');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('email');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('roles');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/profile",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "profile"]
            },
            "description": "Get current user profile information\n\n**Requires:** Valid JWT token\n**Returns:** User profile data with roles and metadata"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Refresh expired access token using refresh token"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "User authentication endpoints for registration, login, and token management"
    },
    {
      "name": "🔄 Workflow Management",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List Workflows",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Workflows retrieved successfully', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "// Auto-set first workflow ID for testing",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (jsonData.data && jsonData.data.length > 0) {",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('workflowId', jsonData.data[0].id);",
                  "        ",
                  "        // Extract trigger path from triggerUrl",
                  "        const triggerUrl = jsonData.data[0].triggerUrl;",
                  "        const triggerPath = triggerUrl.split('/t/')[1];",
                  "        pm.collectionVariables.set('triggerPath', triggerPath);",
                  "        ",
                  "        console.log('✅ Set workflowId:', jsonData.data[0].id);",
                  "        console.log('✅ Set triggerPath:', triggerPath);",
                  "    }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows?page=1&limit=10&enabled=true",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "workflows"],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "page",
                  "value": "1",
                  "description": "Page number for pagination"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "10",
                  "description": "Number of workflows per page"
                },
                {
                  "key": "enabled",
                  "value": "true",
                  "description": "Filter by enabled status"
                },
                {
                  "key": "search",
                  "value": "",
                  "description": "Search by workflow name",
                  "disabled": true
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Get paginated list of user's workflows\n\n**Query Parameters:**\n- page: Page number (default: 1)\n- limit: Items per page (default: 20, max: 100)\n- enabled: Filter by enabled status\n- search: Search by workflow name\n\n**Auto-sets:** workflowId and triggerPath from first result"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Create Workflow",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Workflow created successfully', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('id');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('triggerUrl');",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Workflow structure valid', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.steps).to.be.an('array');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.steps.length).to.be.greaterThan(0);",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Auto-set new workflow ID",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('workflowId', jsonData.data.id);",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Extract trigger path",
                  "    const triggerUrl = jsonData.data.triggerUrl;",
                  "    const triggerPath = triggerUrl.split('/t/')[1];",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('triggerPath', triggerPath);",
                  "    ",
                  "    console.log('✅ Created workflow:', jsonData.data.id);",
                  "    console.log('✅ Trigger URL:', triggerUrl);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman Test Workflow\",\n  \"description\": \"A comprehensive test workflow created via Postman\",\n  \"enabled\": true,\n  \"trigger\": {\n    \"type\": \"http\"\n  },\n  \"steps\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"filter\",\n      \"conditions\": [\n        {\n          \"path\": \"event_type\",\n          \"op\": \"eq\",\n          \"value\": \"user.signup\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"path\": \"user.verified\",\n          \"op\": \"eq\",\n          \"value\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"transform\",\n      \"ops\": [\n        {\n          \"op\": \"template\",\n          \"to\": \"welcome_message\",\n          \"template\": \"Welcome {{user.name}} to our platform! Your email {{user.email}} has been verified.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"op\": \"default\",\n          \"to\": \"priority\",\n          \"value\": \"normal\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"op\": \"pick\",\n          \"to\": \"user_summary\",\n          \"from\": \"user\",\n          \"fields\": [\"id\", \"name\", \"email\"]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"http_request\",\n      \"method\": \"POST\",\n      \"url\": \"https://hooks.slack.com/services/TEST/WEBHOOK/URL\",\n      \"headers\": {\n        \"Content-Type\": \"application/json\",\n        \"X-Source\": \"workflow-engine\"\n      },\n      \"body\": {\n        \"mode\": \"custom\",\n        \"value\": {\n          \"text\": \"{{welcome_message}}\",\n          \"priority\": \"{{priority}}\",\n          \"user\": \"{{user_summary}}\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"retries\": 3,\n      \"timeoutMs\": 5000\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "workflows"]
            },
            "description": "Create a new workflow with comprehensive step configuration\n\n**Features Demonstrated:**\n- Filter step with multiple conditions (AND logic)\n- Transform step with template, default, and pick operations\n- HTTP request step with custom body and headers\n- Retry logic and timeout configuration\n\n**Auto-sets:** workflowId and triggerPath for testing"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get Workflow by ID",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Workflow retrieved successfully', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('id');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data.id).to.equal(pm.collectionVariables.get('workflowId'));",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('Workflow has complete structure', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('steps');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('trigger');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('triggerUrl');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Retrieve a specific workflow by its ID\n\n**Uses:** workflowId variable (set by previous requests)\n**Returns:** Complete workflow configuration with steps and trigger URL"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Update Workflow",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Workflow updated successfully', function () {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data.name).to.include('Updated');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Updated Postman Test Workflow\",\n  \"description\": \"Updated description with new functionality\",\n  \"enabled\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Update workflow properties\n\n**Updatable Fields:**\n- name: Workflow name\n- description: Workflow description\n- enabled: Enable/disable status\n- steps: Complete step configuration\n- trigger: Trigger configuration"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Delete Workflow",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Workflow deleted successfully', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 204]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/{{workflowId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "workflows", "{{workflowId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Delete a workflow permanently\n\n**Warning:** This action cannot be undone\n**Effect:** All associated workflow runs will also be deleted"
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "Complete workflow management operations including CRUD functionality"
    },
    {
      "name": "🚀 Webhook Triggers",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Trigger Workflow - User Signup",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Workflow triggered successfully', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('runId');",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('status');",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    pm.test('Execution completed', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(jsonData.data.status).to.be.oneOf(['success', 'failed', 'skipped']);",
                  "    });",
                  "    ",
                  "    // Auto-set run ID for history testing",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('runId', jsonData.data.runId);",
                  "    ",
                  "    console.log('✅ Workflow executed with status:', jsonData.data.status);",
                  "    console.log('✅ Run ID:', jsonData.data.runId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"event_type\": \"user.signup\",\n  \"user\": {\n    \"id\": \"user_12345\",\n    \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n    \"email\": \"john.doe@example.com\",\n    \"verified\": true,\n    \"signup_date\": \"{{timestamp}}\"\n  },\n  \"source\": \"postman_test\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"{{timestamp}}\",\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"ip_address\": \"192.168.1.100\",\n    \"user_agent\": \"PostmanRuntime/7.32.3\",\n    \"referrer\": \"https://example.com/signup\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/t/{{triggerPath}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["t", "{{triggerPath}}"]
            },
            "description": "Trigger workflow with user signup event\n\n**Payload Features:**\n- Matches filter conditions (event_type: user.signup, user.verified: true)\n- Contains template variables for transformation\n- Includes metadata for comprehensive testing\n\n**Expected Flow:**\n1. Filter: Check event_type and user.verified\n2. Transform: Generate welcome message and user summary\n3. HTTP Request: Send to configured webhook URL\n\n**Auto-sets:** runId for run history testing"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Trigger Workflow - Filtered Out",
          "event": [
